---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms & Conditions | Woodara Design Contest">

    <!-- EN VERSION -->
    <section id="terms" class="section terms">

        <div class="container">

            <div class="terms__content">

                <h2 class="terms__title">
                    Terms & Conditions
                </h2>

                <!-- Блок 1 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        1. General Provisions
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>1.1.</strong>
                        This competition is organized by Woodara (hereinafter referred to as the “Organizer”).
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>1.2.</strong>
                        Participation in this competition is completely free of charge at every stage. The Organizer does not require any registration fees or participation fees from entrants.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>1.3.</strong>
                        This competition is open to Indonesian citizens, including independent furniture designers, architects, students from relevant educational institutions, local artisans, and small design studios.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 2 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        2. Publication & Marketing Rights
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>2.1.</strong>
                        By submitting materials to the official competition website, including but not limited to sketches, technical drawings, 3D renderings, photographs, and concept descriptions, participants grant Woodara a non-exclusive, worldwide, perpetual, and royalty-free license to display, publish, share, and use such materials for promotional, marketing, publication, and communication purposes related to the competition and Woodara’s business activities.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>2.2.</strong>
                        The Organizer reserves the right to publish participants’ work through the official competition website, Woodara’s social media channels, catalogs, presentations, promotional materials, and media publications without any obligation to provide additional financial compensation. In all such cases, the Organizer will continue to credit the designer or studio as the creator and rightful owner of the work.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 3 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        3. Intellectual Property & Winner Agreement
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>3.1.</strong>
                        All copyrights and intellectual property rights related to submitted furniture concepts remain the property of the participant. The Organizer does not claim ownership of designs submitted by participants who are not selected as winners.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>3.2.</strong>
                        Mandatory requirement for finalists: The five (5) participants selected as winners by the jury panel must sign an official commercial agreement with Woodara within seven (7) calendar days of the competition results announcement. This agreement will take the form of an Intellectual Property Assignment & Royalty Agreement.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>3.3.</strong>
                        Under this agreement, winners grant Woodara exclusive rights to manufacture, market, and sell the winning furniture collections worldwide. In return, Woodara will provide the cash prizes outlined in the competition, guarantee ongoing royalty payments for every product sold, and ensure the designer’s name is credited on the product and all relevant marketing materials and official catalogs.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>3.4.</strong>
                        If a winner refuses or fails to sign the official agreement within the specified period, the Organizer reserves the right to revoke the winner’s status and transfer the position to the next highest-ranked participant based on the competition results.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 4 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        4. Code of Conduct
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>4.1.</strong>
                        All submitted works must be original creations owned by the participant. Plagiarism, copying protected furniture designs, or using renderings, images, or materials belonging to third parties without permission is strictly prohibited. Participants bear full personal and legal responsibility for any copyright claims or disputes raised by third parties.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>4.2.</strong>
                        Participants are expected to maintain professional conduct and show respect toward all members of the community within official WhatsApp groups, Telegram groups, and social media discussions related to the competition.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>4.3.</strong>
                        Insults, harassment, defamation, spam, unauthorized promotion of third-party services, or the distribution of misleading or false information regarding other participants, jury members, the Organizer, or Woodara are strictly prohibited.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 5 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        5. Disqualification Without Prior Notice
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>5.1.</strong>
                        The Organizer reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to disqualify participants and remove entries from the website and voting system without prior notice under the following circumstances:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            Evidence of plagiarism or strong grounds to question the originality and ownership of the submitted work.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            Violation of conduct rules, including actions that damage the reputation of the Organizer, jury members, or other participants.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            Attempts to manipulate public voting results, including but not limited to the use of bots, fake accounts, paid voting services, automated click networks, or any other methods intended to influence voting outcomes unfairly.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            Submission of false, incomplete, misleading, or falsified registration information, identity details, or contact information.
                        </li>

                    </ul>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>5.2.</strong>
                        All decisions made by the Organizer regarding disqualification are final, binding, and not subject to dispute, appeal, or further review.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 6 -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        6. Personal Data Protection (UU PDP)
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>6.1.</strong>
                        The collection, processing, storage, and use of participants’ personal data, including names, WhatsApp numbers, email addresses, city of residence, educational background, and employment information, are carried out in accordance with applicable Indonesian laws and regulations, including Personal Data Protection Law No. 27 of 2022.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>6.2.</strong>
                        The Organizer is committed to maintaining the confidentiality of all personal data received and will use it solely for competition administration, official communications, participant verification, voting verification, and protection against abuse and spam.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>6.3.</strong>
                        Participants’ personal data, including telephone numbers and email addresses, will not be shared, sold, or transferred to third parties unless required by law or requested by authorized government authorities.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        <strong>6.4.</strong>
                        Participants may request the deletion of their personal data from Woodara’s systems through an official request submitted to the support team. Such deletion will automatically result in withdrawal from the competition.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>


            <!-- Материалы -->
            <div id="materials" class="terms__materials">

                <div class="terms__materials-heading">

                    <h2 class="terms__materials-title">
                        Material Guidelines for Participants
                    </h2>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        To ensure that all submitted designs can be legally manufactured and exported from Indonesia, participants must use materials that comply with the following requirements.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 1 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        1. Legal & Certified Timber
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Indonesia applies strict regulations regarding the use and export of timber. Therefore, participants may only use wood species that can be supported by official SVLK certification and documentation.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Recommended materials include:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Teak (Jati),</strong>
                            including Perhutani Teak, one of the most sought-after premium materials for export furniture.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Bangkirai,</strong>
                            a highly durable hardwood ideal for outdoor furniture structures.

                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Sonokeling (Indonesian Rosewood),</strong>
                            a premium wood species with distinctive visual character and export regulations.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Mahogany,</strong>
                            ideal for interior furniture and classic design applications.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Mindi (White Cedar),</strong>
                            a lightweight timber commonly used for veneers and interior furniture.
                        </li>

                         <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Suar (Rain Tree),</strong>
                            widely used for solid slab tables.
                        </li>

                    </ul>

                     <p class="terms__text terms__text--warning" >
                        Indonesia enforces strict regulations on the use and export of timber. Therefore, participants may only use wood species that can be supported by official SVLK certification and documentation.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 2 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        2. Natural & Synthetic Rattan
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Indonesia is one of the world’s largest rattan producers and maintains specific regulations regarding its export.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Participants may use:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Natural Rattan</strong>
                            for weaving, decorative panels, headboards, and various furniture applications.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Synthetic (Polymer) Rattan</strong>
                            which offers excellent resistance to weather, humidity, and sunlight, making it highly suitable for outdoor collections.

                        </li>

                    </ul>

                     <p class="terms__text terms__text--warning" >
                        Please note that the export of rattan in raw or semi-processed form is not permitted. Therefore, all designs must be developed as finished furniture products.
                    </p>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 3 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        3. Natural Stone & Minerals
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Participants may incorporate a variety of Indonesian natural stones into their furniture designs to enhance both aesthetic and commercial value.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Recommended materials include:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Indonesian Marble</strong>
                            for tabletops, table bases, and decorative details.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Onyx,</strong>
                            a premium natural stone often used for decorative and backlit applications.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Travertine,</strong>
                            a material widely used in contemporary furniture and interior design.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Terrazzo,</strong>
                            a composite material offering extensive possibilities for form and finishing.
                        </li>

                    </ul>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 4 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        4. Metal Materials
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        The use of metal is permitted without specific restrictions for finished furniture products.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Recommended materials include:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Brass</strong>
                            for hardware, decorative accents, and premium details.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Stainless Steel</strong>
                            for modern and contemporary furniture.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Powder-Coated Aluminum,</strong>
                            a lightweight and corrosion-resistant material ideal for outdoor furniture structures.
                        </li>

                    </ul>

                </div>

                <!-- Блок 5 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        5. Textiles & Upholstery Materials
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Participants may use a wide range of textile materials suitable for their design concepts.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Recommended materials include:
                    </p>

                    <ul class="terms__list">

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Outdoor Fabrics</strong>
                            with protection against water, humidity, and UV exposure.
                        </li>

                        <li class="terms__item">
                            <strong>Natural Linen, Canvas,</strong>
                            and various Indonesian textile materials suitable for upholstery and cushions.
                        </li>
                        
                    </ul>

                </div>

                 <!-- Блок 6 материалы -->
                <div class="terms__block">

                    <h5 class="terms__heading">
                        6. Important Notes
                    </h5>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        Woodara will manage all certification and documentation processes required for manufacturing and export, including SVLK/V-Legal requirements when necessary.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text">
                        However, all participants must use materials that are legal, traceable, and compliant with applicable Indonesian regulations.
                    </p>

                    <p class="terms__text terms__text--warning" >
                        The use of protected timber species, illegal raw materials, or materials without proper documentation will result in the design being ineligible for production or further development.
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>

    </section>

</Layout>

    <style>
        
        .terms {
            padding: 8rem 0;
            background-color: #f9f9f9;
        }

        .container {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 140rem;
            padding: 0 2rem;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .terms__content,
        .terms__materials {
            max-width: 100rem;
        }

        .terms__title {
            color: #111;
            font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 5vw, 5.4rem);
            font-weight: 300;
            line-height: 1.12;
            letter-spacing: -0.04em;
            margin-bottom: 6rem;
        }

        .terms__materials-title {
            color: #111;
            font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 5vw, 5.4rem);
            font-weight: 300;
            line-height: 1.12;
            letter-spacing: -0.04em;
            margin:8rem 0 2rem;
            
        }

        .terms__materials-heading {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            margin-bottom: 6rem;
        }

        .terms__block {
            margin-bottom: 5rem;
        }

        .terms__heading {
            color: #111;
            letter-spacing: -0.02rem;
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }

        .terms__text {
            color: #888;
            font-size: 1.6rem;
            line-height: 1.7;
            margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
        }

        .terms__text:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        .terms__text strong {
            color: #111;
            font-weight: 500;
        }

        .terms__list {
            list-style-type: circle;
            margin: 1.6rem 0;
            padding-left: 2.4rem;
        }

        .terms__item {
            color: #888;
            font-size: 1.6rem;
            line-height: 1.7;
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        .terms__item strong {
            color: #111;
        }

        .terms__text--warning {
            color: #111;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {

            .terms {
                padding: 5rem 0;
            }

            .terms__title {
                font-size: 3.2rem;
                line-height: 1.2;
                margin-bottom: 4rem;
            }

            .terms__block {
                margin-bottom: 4rem;
            }

            .terms__heading {
                font-size: 2rem;
                margin-bottom: 2rem;
            }

            .terms__text {
                font-size: 1.4rem;
                line-height: 1.6;
            }

        }

    </style>